ve\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}^{2} & -1 \\\\ {x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}} & {e}^{{x}_{1}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe linear approximation of $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n1+(-1)+1=1.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367833 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186367834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367833 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186367835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367833 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186367836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367833 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186367837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367833 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186367838 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367833 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367833 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367833 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186367836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367833 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "703aea1e-c64a-581f-b4f6-a53c00907653" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367834 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367834 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367834 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2bc8f2d1-ecfb-50d7-b14b-04f9786d82ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367835 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367835 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367835 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5f7d0746-3536-5992-9206-08d262d180df" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367836 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/re