 n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂z}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{xyz})=yz{e}^{xyz},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{xyz})=xz{e}^{xyz},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{xyz})=xy{e}^{xyz} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+yz)=1,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x+yz)=z,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x+yz)=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}yz{e}^{xyz} & xz{e}^{xyz} & xy{e}^{xyz} \\\\ 1 & z & y\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401413 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401414 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401413 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401415 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401413 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401416 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401413 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401417 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401413 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401418 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401413 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401413 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401413 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186401417 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401413 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9cbe7815-5a90-5779-9948-27720bbf467a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401414 #edb/ref 1080 "$x{e}^{xyz},\\,$ $z,\\,$ and $z$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [